  "id": "COMPOUND:17561 - PROTEIN:6020",
  "verbalization": "Maytansine, N(2')-deacetyl-N(2')-(3-methyl-1-oxobutyl)- is implicated in targeting PITSLRE serine/threonine-protein kinase CDC2L1 through a series of intermediate targets. The evidence suggests that Maytansine interacts with G2/mitotic-specific cyclin B1, which is a known target of 2,3,5,8-Tetramethyldecane and Npc185762. These compounds, in turn, direct activity toward CDC2L1. The presence of multiple pathways converging on CDC2L1 indicates a potential role for Maytansine in modulating the activity of this kinase, possibly through the regulation of cyclin B1. The integration of these targets highlights a possible mechanism by which Maytansine influences cellular processes involving the G2/mitotic phase, potentially through the regulation of cyclin B1 and its downstream targets. The evidence supports a functional link between Maytansine and CDC2L1, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
